# Operations Guide — {{project_slug}}

This is the user-facing manual for installing, running, checking, and troubleshooting the app.

User-facing guides are organized under `docs/user-manual/`. When sharing instructions with the user, always show the exact guide path.

## Install

```bash
composer install
npm install
cp .env.example .env
php artisan key:generate
php artisan migrate
npm run build
```

Use `docs/Handsoff/env-guide.md` to fill `.env` values.

Sandbox review uses normal login with seeded test credentials. Use `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md` to find the email/username and password for each role/persona needed to test the full app flow.

## Run locally

```bash
php artisan serve
npm run dev
php artisan queue:work
```

If the app uses Horizon:

```bash
php artisan horizon
```

## Run sandbox

The sandbox is managed through:

```text
docs/Handsoff/bootstrap-sandbox.md
```

After it succeeds:

```bash
cat docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt
cat docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-runbook.md
```

During `/larv:full`, `/larv:feature`, `/larv:debug`, or handoff implementation, the AI is responsible for running Laravel commands and restarting/probing the sandbox. The user should only need to open the public URL and test the app.

## Verify

```bash
vendor/bin/pint --test
vendor/bin/pest
vendor/bin/phpstan analyse
npm run build
```

Smoke test:

```bash
curl -fsS "$(cat docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt)" >/dev/null
```

When the AI changes code, it must decide and run the needed runtime commands: migrations, seeders, `php artisan optimize:clear`, `npm run build`, queue/Horizon/runtime restarts, and `docs/larv/07-runtime/deploy-sandbox.sh` if the public sandbox needs refresh.

